    "title": "Guilford County — the money trail",
    "grand_total": 889196646,
    "year": 2027,
    "note": "Guilford County (Greensboro and High Point), the third-most-populous county in North Carolina. This tree is the General Fund — the main operating budget, $889.2 million — shown by department, from the county’s adopted budget book. Counting every fund (debt service, school capital, rural fire, grants), the all-funds budget is about $1.19 billion. The property tax rate is 78.95¢ per $100. Every figure ties to the adopted budget book’s own summary tables, which foot to the dollar."
